Problem description
- There is a set of cities $$\mathcal{N}$$ indexed by $$i,j \in \mathcal{N}$$, with a designated start and end city $$s \in \mathcal{N}$$.
- Travel costs are given by a cost matrix $$D \in \mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{N}| \times |\mathcal{N}|}$$, where $$D_{ij}$$ is the distance or travel cost from city $$i$$ to city $$j$$.
- The planning horizon is a single closed tour, represented by visit positions $$k \in \mathcal{K} = \{1,\ldots,|\mathcal{N}|\}$$.
- Each city has a unit visit requirement $$r_i$$, meaning every city must be included exactly once in the tour.
- The planning goal is to minimize the total travel distance of the complete closed route.
- The route must start at $$s$$, visit every city exactly once, and return to $$s$$.
- No city may be skipped, repeated, or visited more than once.
- The selected travel links must form one continuous tour and must not contain disconnected subtours.
- The travel-cost data may be asymmetric, so $$D_{ij}$$ and $$D_{ji}$$ may differ.
- No capacity, inventory, workforce, or demand-allocation limits are present beyond the single-visit requirement for each city.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$\pi_k$$: the city visited at route position $$k$$.
  - $$x_{ij}$$: a binary indicator showing whether direct travel from city $$i$$ to city $$j$$ is used.
  - $$L$$: the total distance of the selected closed tour.

Input Format
{
  "n": {
    "type": "integer",
    "description": "Number of cities in $$\\mathcal{N}$$."
  },
  "s": {
    "type": "integer",
    "description": "Index of the designated start and end city $$s$$."
  },
  "D": {
    "type": "matrix",
    "shape": "[$$n$$, $$n$$]",
    "description": "Travel cost matrix $$D$$, where $$D_{ij}$$ is the direct travel cost from city $$i$$ to city $$j$$."
  },
  "r": {
    "type": "vector",
    "shape": "[$$n$$]",
    "description": "Required visit counts $$r_i$$ for each city; in the standard TSP setting, each entry is unit-valued."
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "route": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "[$$n+1$$]",
    "description": "Ordered list of city indices representing the closed tour; the first and last entries are $$s$$."
  },
  "selected_arcs": {
    "type": "matrix",
    "shape": "[$$n$$, $$n$$]",
    "description": "Binary travel-selection matrix $$X$$, where $$X_{ij} = 1$$ if the tour goes directly from city $$i$$ to city $$j$$, and $$0$$ otherwise."
  },
  "total_distance": {
    "type": "number",
    "description": "Total travel distance of the selected tour."
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "n": 4,
  "s": 1,
  "D": [
    [0, 10, 20, 12],
    [10, 0, 5, 10],
    [20, 5, 0, 8],
    [15, 12, 8, 0]
  ],
  "r": [1, 1, 1, 1]
}
